// ImportDemo: TEST ONLY. The demonstration of scripts/fp127/gen.py's
// `@import`, which lets one library's source call another's functions under
// a prefix (FP127.yul.src takes FP19's wide kernels this way). Nothing here
// ships: gen.py --lib import-demo emits ImportDemoLib.sol beside this file,
// make gen-check keeps it current, and test/fp127/Imports.t.sol checks it.
//
// Three exports, each a call into another source through the imports below:
//   * wexpm1, FP19's wide e^r - 1 kernel itself (with its helpers wmul,
//     wdivs, mulwu, wdbl, ...), checked against mpmath's e^r - 1;
//   * expm1, FP19's whole expm1 export (its fast path, its rounding test
//     and its second stage, some thirty functions with msb, rev and the
//     other helpers FP127.yul.src also defines), which must return the
//     word FP19Lib.expm1 returns, and revert where and as it reverts;
//   * rbad127, FP127.yul.src's rounding test (unused there until a phase
//     calls it), checked against the rounding it describes.
// Every function of each closure arrives renamed <alias>_<name>, its calls
// with it; the errors FP19's code reverts with are declared here, as the
// importer must.

/// @error Overflow() 0x35278d12
/// @error DivisionByZero() 0x23d359a3
/// @error OutOfRange() 0x7db3aba7

/// @import fp19 as w19: wexpm1, fp19_expm1
/// @import fp127 as f127: rbad127

/// @export wexpm1(uint256 rh, uint256 rl) returns (uint256 eh, uint256 el)
/// @domain r = (rh 2^256 + rl) 2^-510 in [0, 1)
/// @reverts nothing
/// @notice FP19's w19_wexpm1: e^r - 1 in two words at 2^-510, within
///         2^-503.
function demo_wexpm1(rh, rl) -> eh, el {
    eh, el := w19_wexpm1(rh, rl)
}

/// @export expm1(int256 x) returns (int256 r)
/// @domain any FP19 word, as FP19Lib.expm1
/// @reverts as FP19Lib.expm1
/// @notice FP19's w19_fp19_expm1: FP19Lib.expm1's own body, imported.
function demo_expm1(x) -> r {
    r := w19_fp19_expm1(x)
}

/// @export rbad127(uint256 v, uint256 g, uint256 err) returns (uint256 b)
/// @domain 1 <= g <= 256
/// @reverts nothing
/// @notice FP127's f127_rbad127: 1 when v +- err, with g guard bits, may
///         round to another word than v under FP127's tie rule.
function demo_rbad127(v, g, err) -> b {
    b := f127_rbad127(v, g, err)
}
